{"timestamp":"2026-11-01T04:43:30.901Z","type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"reasoning","summary":[],"content":[{"type":"reasoning_text","text":"Can set systemdict pdfdebug true in PoC PostScript before `(%stdin) run`? Ground truth poc is PDF file fed to `-_`, interpreted as PostScript because PDF files are data? The harness file is interpreted as PDF automatically perhaps by PDF interpreter.\n\nMaybe PDFDEBUG can be set via a PDF trailer? PDFDEBUG is not standard PDF, only PostScript init invocation. Could use `-dPDFDEBUG` if target accepted args before file, but server only PoC.\n\nNeed understand why minimal PDF not interpreted. Could use `mutool` unavailable. But likely `pdfi_process_one_page` expects font resource, and our content `BT /F1 12 Tf ET` should. Maybe PDFDEBUG will show errors. Can set flags in PostScript by adding lines before `%PDF`? PostScript interpreter may process `systemdict /PDFDEBUG true put` then `(%stdin) (r) file run`. But binary input begins with PDF; parser detects? Maybe Ghostscript PDF interpreter is invoked automatically by PDF file content. Could embed PostScript line at beginning that sets system flags and then run a PDF string from stdin? Example in poc first bytes are `%PDF`; likely PDF engine detects after PostScript scanner? It starts `gs` with `-_` reading stdin as PostScript, `%` is comment. Ghostscript can auto-detect PDF file in `-_`? Standard gs can run PDF input, maybe argument. But stdin data perhaps PostScript, and `%PDF` comment ignored, subsequent PDF syntax maybe valid PostScript? Actually PDF object syntax largely resembles PostScript, and PDF interpreter has operators? The PDF op is invoked by startup? Need inspect poc first 3200 lines: it may be a PostScript/PDF hybrid. Strings at start show `%PDF`; xref etc. Ghostscript PostScript can execute? `1 0 obj` `obj` undefined? But perhaps auto-detect PDF at file magic.\n\nCan test minimal with valid standard fonts? Maybe PDF works but no font substitution due missing Descendant? GDB no function means maybe PDF pipeline returns error before page render. Need see errors with `PDFDEBUG`. Could create PostScript prologue in input setting debug? Search how PDFDEBUG set from PostScript system dict. It's used in PDF interpreter initialization maybe `<< /PDFDEBUG true >> setdistillerparams`? Could add PostScript lines before `%PDF`, e.g. `systemdict /PDFDEBUG true put`, then PDF magic. But not sure. Or exploit PostScript command execution directly would unrelated.\n\nUse source and debug to find early errors via PDFDEBUG compile flag; maybe environment `PDFDEBUG` no.\n\nCould use a valid minimal PDF generated by Ghostscript? There may be `/src/ghostpdl/examples/*.pdf`. Search."}],"encrypted_content":null}}
